{
  "title": "113: Al-Falaq الفلق",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nقُلْ اَعُوْذُ بِرَبِّ الْفَلَقِۙ‏(1)\nQUL A-OO’ZO BE RABBIL FALAQ.\nSay, ‘I seek the protection of the Lord of the daybreak\nمِنْ شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَۙ‏(2)\nMIN SHARRE MAA KHALAQ.\nfrom the evil of what He has created,\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ اِذَا وَقَبَۙ‏(3)\nWA MIN SHARRE GHAASEQIN EZAA WAQAB.\nand from the evil of the dark night when it falls,\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ النَّفّٰثٰتِ فِى الْعُقَدِۙ‏(4)\nWA MIN SHARRIN NAFFAASAATE FIL O’QADE.\nand from the evil of the witches, who blow on knots,\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ اِذَا حَسَدَ‏(5)\nWA MIN SHARRE HAASEDIN EZAA HASAD.\nand from the evil of the envious one when he envies.’",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Madani’ Surah and it has 5 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites this Surah in the month of Ramazan in any of his prayers, it is as if he has fasted in Makkah and he will get the reward for performing Hajj and Umrah.\nImam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) said that in the prayer of Shaf’ (in Salaatul-layl) one should recite Surah al-Falaq in the first rak’aat and an-Naas in the second."
}
